ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":146,"prev":148,"next":151,"titles":153,"firmware":27},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":13,"order":14,"path":15,"context":16,"summary":20,"status":21,"firmware":22,"facts":28,"procedures":91,"parameters":101,"related":124,"body":128,"sources":129,"official_url":32,"controls":139},"instrument.filter","Filter (M3)",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"filter page","cutoff","resonance","filter type","lowpass","highpass","ladder filter","key tracking","instrument",30,"knowledge/manual/units/instrument/filter.md",{"modes":17,"screens":18},[13],[19],"M3","`M3` is the track's filter: cutoff, resonance, filter-envelope amount and key tracking. `shift + M3` picks the type — ladder, svf, z hipass or z lowpass, with dynamic above them from OS 1.2 — and then returns to `M1`.","current",{"min":23,"changed_in":24,"guide_version":26,"verified_on":27},"1.0.9",[25],"1.2.0","1.1.15","1.1.33",[29,35,38,43,48,51,55,58,61,64,67,71,75,79,82,85,88],{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"purpose","The filter takes away part of the frequency range and can emphasise the frequencies around its cutoff.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/instrument#filter",null,"official",{"id":36,"text":37,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"type","`shift + M3` opens the choice of filter types, each with its own character.",{"id":39,"text":40,"source":41,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"type-names","The type list, headed with the track number and the word filter, offers ladder, svf, z hipass and z lowpass, the current one boxed.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#23-filter-instrument-m3","verified",{"id":44,"text":45,"source":46,"firmware_min":25,"verified_on":33,"confidence":47},"type-names-os12","On OS 1.2 the type list has a fifth entry, dynamic, above ladder, so ladder sits one detent down from the top; see the dynamic filter unit.","docs/research/79b-os12-small-features.md#1-dynamic-filter-120","community-verified",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":41,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"type-return","Picking a type takes you back to the engine page (`M1`); `M3` then shows the new type.",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":54,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":47},"on-off","Presets also store whether the filter is switched on at all.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#25-fx-m3-filter-and-lfo-m4",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":41,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"off","With the filter off, the page is dimmed under an off box; pressing `M3` again switches the filter on.",{"id":59,"text":60,"source":41,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"screen","The page draws the filter's curve over tinted bands, with the type name at the top left, a frequency axis marked 50, 1k, 2k, 5k and 20kHz, and a small black box on the curve that shows the resonance, 00–99, rising as resonance goes up.",{"id":62,"text":63,"source":41,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"drawn","Cutoff slides the curve's slope along the axis, key tracking moves an arrow along the bottom from left to right, and any envelope amount above 0 adds a hatched ghost of the curve to its right; z hipass mirrors the drawing.",{"id":65,"text":66,"source":41,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"env-range","Envelope amount runs from none at 0 to full at 99; there is no negative setting that would sweep the cutoff down.",{"id":68,"text":69,"source":70,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"midi-ccs","Over MIDI, CC32–35 on the track's channel move cutoff, resonance, envelope amount and key tracking, and the page redraws as they arrive.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#3-midi-reach-on-1133-verified-on-screen",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":74,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":47},"no-type-cc","No MIDI CC is known for the filter type.","docs/research/20-midi-control.md#33-instrument-tracks-18-synth-drum-sampler-multisampler-engines",{"id":76,"text":77,"source":78,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"types-sound","Ladder and svf are 24 dB lowpasses modelled on analog circuits: the ladder four stages with feedback, the bass thinning as resonance rises; the svf two state-variable stages with a soft knee at resonance 0. z lowpass and z hipass are single two-pole digital filters, very gentle at resonance 0; the z lowpass rises to a whistling, nearly self-oscillating peak while the z hipass only reaches a mild one.","docs/research/60-sound-session.md#2-filters",{"id":80,"text":81,"source":78,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"cutoff-range","Cutoff spans from about 25 Hz to past 20 kHz; at the same setting the z hipass sits an octave below the z lowpass, and the svf a little above the ladder.",{"id":83,"text":84,"source":78,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"svf-shift","On the svf, raising resonance also lowers the peak by up to about half an octave and takes away up to 9 dB of level.",{"id":86,"text":87,"source":78,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"key-tracking-law","Key tracking pivots on C2: at 0 the cutoff ignores the note, at the middle it follows half an octave per octave, at the top an octave per octave.",{"id":89,"text":90,"source":78,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":27,"confidence":42},"env-amount-law","At the envelope's peak, envelope amount opens the cutoff by about 0.85 of its own steps on the cutoff's scale, so a full amount from a closed filter opens it almost all the way.",[92],{"id":36,"goal":93,"preconditions":94,"steps":97,"result":33,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"Change the filter type of the selected track",[95,96],"instrument mode","the track is selected",[98],{"keys":99,"note":100,"set":33},"shift + M3","opens the filter types",[102,108,113,119],{"screen":19,"encoder":103,"layer":104,"keys":105,"name":6,"range":33,"default":33,"cc":106,"cc_confidence":47,"note":107,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"E1","base","turn E1",32,"frequency where the filter acts",{"screen":19,"encoder":109,"layer":104,"keys":110,"name":7,"range":33,"default":33,"cc":111,"cc_confidence":47,"note":112,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"E2","turn E2",33,"peak at the cutoff that exaggerates the filter",{"screen":19,"encoder":114,"layer":104,"keys":115,"name":116,"range":33,"default":33,"cc":117,"cc_confidence":47,"note":118,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"E3","turn E3","envelope amount",34,"how far the `M2` filter envelope sweeps the cutoff",{"screen":19,"encoder":120,"layer":104,"keys":121,"name":12,"range":33,"default":33,"cc":122,"cc_confidence":47,"note":123,"source":32,"firmware_min":33,"verified_on":33,"confidence":34},"E4","turn E4",35,"ties the cutoff to the pitch of each note",[125,126,127],"instrument.envelopes","instrument.track-sends","instrument.lfo","The filter is a track's main tone control. Lower the cutoff to darken a sound, add resonance for a\nsharper edge, and raise envelope amount so the filter envelope sweeps the cutoff on every note — the\nclassic plucky bass. The shift layer of this page holds the track's sends, not filter settings.",[130,132,134,135,136,137,138],{"url":32,"kind":131},"guide",{"url":41,"kind":133},"research",{"url":46,"kind":133},{"url":54,"kind":133},{"url":70,"kind":133},{"url":74,"kind":133},{"url":78,"kind":133},[140,141,142,143,144,145],"key.shift","key.m3","encoder.1","encoder.2","encoder.3","encoder.4",{"id":13,"title":147},"Instrument",{"id":149,"title":150},"instrument.play-mode","Play mode, portamento, bend range and preset volume (M2 + shift)",{"id":126,"title":152},"Track sends to aux out, tape, FX I and FX II (M3 + shift)",{"basics.key-notation":154,"basics.main-modes":155,"basics.modules":156,"basics.track-buttons":157,"basics.linked-tracks":158,"basics.patterns-scenes-son